## Report
Validated the finding. I created a minimal Rust Cargo example at crates/auth/examples/head_bucket_bypass.rs that constructs an explicit Deny bucket policy for s3:ListBucket with Condition Null:{"s3:prefix":"true"}. It evaluates two requests: (1) the contextless HeadBucket-like request built as PolicyRequest::for_bucket(...).with_absent_request_headers(), and (2) a control request that additionally marks list parameters absent with with_prefix(None), with_delimiter(None), and with_max_keys(None). The PoC output was: contextless_decision=NoMatch; fixed_absent_list_context_decision=ExplicitDeny; contextless_head_bucket_allowed_with_public_read_fallback=true; fixed_head_bucket_allowed_with_public_read_fallback=false. This demonstrates that the explicit Deny is skipped only for the contextless path and that a public-read/ACL fallback would allow the HeadBucket-style authorization. Code evidence: PolicyRequest::for_bucket leaves prefix/delimiter/max_keys as RequestField::Unavailable at crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs:399-401; with_absent_request_headers only marks request headers absent and does not touch list parameters at crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs:551-564. s3:prefix, s3:delimiter, and s3:max-keys are supported ListBucket condition keys at crates/auth/src/bucket_policy/condition_key.rs:280-303 and list_condition_supported_for_action includes PolicyAction::ListBucket at lines 603-607. Those keys resolve through request_field_to_resolved at lines 441-450, where RequestField::Unavailable becomes ResolvedValue::Unavailable at lines 468-473. evaluate_clause returns ConditionMatchResult::InputUnavailable for that case at lines 719-723, and PolicyStatement::request_effect maps InputUnavailable to None even for Deny at crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs:786-790. The HeadBucket authorization path evaluates ListBucket through bucket_policy_decision_for_loaded_handle at crates/server-core/src/coordinator/authz/bucket.rs:58-75; that helper builds the contextless request with only with_absent_request_headers at crates/server-core/src/coordinator/authz/policy.rs:268-280. bucket_policy_allows_with_fallback sends NoMatch to fallback at crates/server-core/src/coordinator/authz/policy.rs:474-482. Dynamic/debugger evidence: cargo run -p auth --example head_bucket_bypass reproduced the bypass. I attempted crash-style validation; the issue is a logic bug and did not crash. Valgrind was not installed, and ASan could not be used because -Z sanitizer=address requires nightly Rust. I then ran lldb non-interactively and hit condition_key.rs:723 followed by bucket_policy.rs:790; the backtrace showed the call chain condition_key::evaluate_clause -> PolicyStatement::condition_match_result -> PolicyStatement::request_effect -> BucketPolicy::evaluate -> head_bucket_bypass.rs:51, confirming the unavailable prefix becomes InputUnavailable and is then treated as no policy effect.

